\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Continuum displacements and single-sided matter}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{In the same revised version of \citef{lasenby1998gravity},
Section 3.2, equations (3.33)–(3.34), p. 21, concern displacement
covariance of the continuum connection. Section 3.3, equations
(3.43)–(3.46), p. 23, also changes the integration measure and
boundary of the domain. These are additional continuum data;
a vertex translation of the [rotational cochains](fdip-00YN)
supplies none of them.}

\p{Section 3.3, equations (3.48)–(3.50), p. 24, uses a
single-sided rotor action for spinor matter, in contrast to the
multivector action in \ref{fdip-00Z4}. Its full coupled derivative
and action are (3.55)–(3.56), p. 24. This comparison makes no
choice between spinor and exterior matter on the finite complex,
and provides no transformation of the fixed finite site set.}
